WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.592
Before scaling up to a large language model, start with one neuron.

00:00:04.592 --> 00:00:13.962
A neuron takes numeric inputs, multiplies them by learned weights, adds a bias, and then applies an activation function.

00:00:13.962 --> 00:00:16.687
Use the numbers in the diagram.

00:00:16.687 --> 00:00:25.532
X one is two, X two is one, weight one is zero point five, weight two is negative zero point two,

00:00:25.532 --> 00:00:28.257
and the bias is zero point one.

00:00:28.257 --> 00:00:31.507
The weighted sum becomes zero point nine.

00:00:31.507 --> 00:00:36.877
Re L U keeps that positive value, so the hidden output is zero point nine.

00:00:37.419 --> 00:00:40.576
The important idea is not the arithmetic itself.

00:00:40.576 --> 00:00:47.666
A weight is a learned number that controls how strongly an input contributes to the next computation.

00:00:47.666 --> 00:00:55.811
An L L M contains vastly more learned parameters, but this weighted-transformation idea is still underneath the larger

00:00:55.811 --> 00:00:57.263
architecture.
